{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And I will bless you.</b> I Myself, in My glory." "<b>And I will magnify your name.</b> That I will add one letter to your name, for the count of 248 limbs, and it will be found a complete body and a complete name." "<b>And you shall be a blessing.</b> Your blessing precedes My blessing — that they say at the beginning מג\"א and afterward מחיה המתים. Another interpretation: והיה ברכה — until now the blessings were in My hand; from now on they are given over into your hand, and you shall bless whomever you wish. And when He wished to bless Isaac, He saw that Esau was destined to come forth from him, and He did not wish to bless. He said: I will wait until the One who gave the blessings to me comes and blesses him if He wishes. Thus it is written: ״ויהי אחרי מות אברהם ויברך אלהים את יצחק בנו״. A parable: to a king who had a beautiful orchard and gave it over to his friend to guard and to water it. The guard began to stroll in it and saw there two trees — one producing deadly poison and one producing the elixir of life — and both needed watering, and he could not water one without the other. He said: What should I do? If I water the good one, I will be keeping the evil one alive; and if I do not water, the good one will die. He went back and said: I will leave everything until the owner of the orchard comes and does as he wishes. Another interpretation: והיה ברכה — an expression of command, that He commanded him that wherever he goes he should teach people to recognize their Creator and bless Him. And so he did, as it is written further on: ״ויקרא בשם ה׳״ — that the Creator, may He be exalted, said to him, and they did not recognize Him. And therefore: ״ויהי רעב בארץ״."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:05:20.824356069Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}